# What a deploy installs, root-owned, for the session (and the program that puts each application in a
# scope of its own, docs/adr/0066-quality-of-service.mdx), the login, the accounts and the PIN (docs/adr/0020-oxy-account-login.mdx,
# "Installing on a machine"; docs/adr/0010-lock-screen.mdx; docs/adr/0054-recovery-and-erasing.mdx), and for
# Safe Mode on a converted machine (ADR 0054, decision 10: the recovery's program, which writes its boot
# entries, OxyOS's kernel-install plugin and the polkit rule), and for backups (docs/adr/0059-backups.mdx:
# the backup service and its units, the migration's socket and service), and for memory
# (docs/adr/0066-quality-of-service.mdx, decision 7: zswap and MGLRU set at boot, the session's and
# the user manager's slices' protections, systemd-oomd on the applications' slice), read by
# tools/deploy/remote.sh.
# tools/deploy/system-files.py checks it against the tree: every binary, unit, PAM service, sysusers and
# tmpfiles file of tools/oxyos-session, tools/oxyos-login and tools/oxyos-accountd is here, every PAM file
# where its own header says it is installed, the recovery's program, every kernel-install plugin of
# tools/oxyos-recovery and every polkit rule of config/, each where the image installs it, the backup
# service's program where its units start it and every unit of tools/oxyos-backupd, and every
# drop-in, tmpfiles and modules-load file of config/'s, each where the image installs it. A FROM in
# target/release/ is built there (by its tool's package).
# FROM                                                                  TO                                              MODE
